### Tripletex API — employee lookup
### Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension (or JetBrains HTTP client).
### Run request 1 first, copy the returned session token into @sessionToken below.

@baseUrl = https://tripletex.no/v2
@consumerToken = ...
@employeeToken = ...
@expirationDate = 2026-05-22

### 1. Create a session token (no auth required)
# @name session
PUT {{baseUrl}}/token/session/:create?consumerToken={{consumerToken}}&employeeToken={{employeeToken}}&expirationDate={{expirationDate}}

### --- After request 1 succeeds, paste session.value.token here ---
@sessionToken = ...session.value.token..

### Basic auth header: base64("0:<sessionToken>"). REST Client computes this from the values above.

### 2. List all employees (id, firstName, lastName, email)
GET {{baseUrl}}/employee?from=0&count=1000&fields=id,firstName,lastName,email
Authorization: Basic 0:{{sessionToken}}

### 3. Look up a single employee by email
GET {{baseUrl}}/employee?email=andreas.rodland@fink.no&fields=id,firstName,lastName,email
Authorization: Basic 0:{{sessionToken}}

### 4. Whoami — confirm which tenant/company the token belongs to
GET {{baseUrl}}/token/session/>whoAmI
Authorization: Basic 0:{{sessionToken}}
